.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NOQTIS-BOX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm noqtis-box
.Nd seal a file of any size to ML-KEM public keys
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm noqtis box
.Fl p Ar key.pub
.Op Fl p Ar key.pub ...
.Fl o Ar out
.Op Fl c Ar ctx
.Op Fl s Ar key Op Fl -pass-fd Ar n | Fl -pass-env Ar name
.Op Fl -chunk Ar bytes
.Op Fl f | Fl -force
.Ar file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm noqtis box
encrypts
.Ar file
(or standard input for
.Ar - )
so that only the holder of the secret key of
.Ar key.pub ,
an ML-KEM-512, -768 or -1024 key, can read it with
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1 ,
and writes the result to
.Ar out
(or standard output for
.Ar - ) .
The format is noqtis-kstream-1
.Pq Xr nqkfeini 3 :
a header holding an ML-KEM ciphertext, then the file in chunks, each
under ChaCha20-Poly1305 with its own nonce, so that changed, moved,
repeated or dropped chunks and a cut stream are all detected.
It reads and writes one chunk at a time, whatever the file's size.
.Pp
With
.Fl p
given more than once, or with
.Fl s ,
the format is noqtis-kstream-2
.Pq Xr nqkmeini 3 :
the same chunks under a random file key, which the header carries once
for each recipient, so that any one of their secret keys opens it.
A changed header, another recipient's part of it included, fails for
every recipient.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl p Ar key.pub , Fl -pub Ns = Ns Ar key.pub
The recipient's ML-KEM public key file.
Given up to 32 times, each key a recipient; the keys may be of
different ML-KEM sets.
.It Fl s Ar key , Fl -sign Ns = Ns Ar key
Sign the file with the secret signature key
.Ar key
(any algorithm
.Xr noqtis-algs 1
lists for signatures).
The signature is over the header and the whole file, and is inside the
encryption: only a recipient learns who signed, and because it covers
the recipients, one of them cannot pass the file on as if the sender had
sealed it to someone else.
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1
checks it with
.Fl s .
.It Fl -pass-fd Ar n , Fl -pass-env Ar name
The passphrase of a protected
.Fl s
key, as in
.Xr noqtis-sign 1 .
.It Fl o Ar out , Fl -out Ns = Ns Ar out
The output file, or
.Ar -
for standard output.
.It Fl c Ar ctx , Fl -ctx Ns = Ns Ar ctx
A context string (at most 255 bytes) that
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1
must be given too.
.It Fl -chunk Ar bytes
The chunk size, 1024 to 16777216 (default 65536).
.It Fl f , Fl -force
Replace an existing output file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 2 on a usage, key or file error; an output file is
removed when the command fails or is stopped by a signal (it is written
under a temporary name and renamed once whole,
.Xr noqtis 1 ) .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis keygen -a ML-KEM-768 -o box
$ noqtis box -p box.pub -o data.nqk data.csv
$ noqtis unbox -k box -o data.csv data.nqk
.Ed
.Pp
To two people, signed:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ noqtis box -p ann.pub -p bob.pub -s me -o data.nqk data.csv
$ noqtis unbox -k bob -s me.pub -o data.csv data.nqk
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-keygen 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-unbox 1 ,
.Xr nqkfeini 3 ,
.Xr nqkmeini 3
